{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"DECISION (operator): **descope safe-run batching from this story** — Option 1 of the three recorded in the previous comment. The plan and ACs have been updated accordingly.\n\nRationale, as recorded by the operator: the measurements show batching's real benefit is ~12% fewer pandoc spawns (the 74% ceiling is unreachable because 46% of runs are single-unit) while changing rendered output on ~12% of corpus bodies. That is a bad trade, and **output divergence is exactly the class of behaviour change to escalate rather than ship silently**. Option 2 would have pinned that divergence as intended, which is not wanted; Option 3 would spend investigation to, at best, restore equivalence for the same 12%.\n\n**Kept (uncontested, all still in scope):** the caller-side wall-clock timeout, process-group reaping via `rebar._proc.reap_process_group`, the existing PER-UNIT fallback semantics, the `reconciler.dc_pandoc_timeout_s` config surface, the wheel pin + CI check, and the new repo-root `NOTICE` recording pandoc's GPL entry.\n\n**The spawn tax is not being ignored** — it is properly addressed by the cutover story `[rebar:3388-96e8-e14e-4221]`'s change-gated `rich_sha` skip, which avoids rendering unchanged bodies at all. That is a far larger win than 12% for the same hazard.\n\nA new AC was added to make the reduced scope falsifiable: rendered output must be **byte-identical to the landed renderer across the whole committed 178-body corpus**, proving this story changes robustness only, never rendering.\n\nFollow-up idea ticket filed for the spawn-cost question, carrying the 21-divergent-bodies analysis as its starting point, linked `discovered_from` this story."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786596709381431001,"uuid":"f3d95506-2145-4877-a0a3-320a5a8fc154"}